 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "One verse of 140 s (never cut). No people drawn (scribe, witnesses): hourglass for the term, pen for writing, scales for justice in writing (worldly justice, not the Mizan), seal for witnessing (twice), scroll, coins for present trade and the sale, a lamp for taqwa. 282:108-115 (witnessing a sale, harm to/by scribes) not glossed: the tafsirs give more than one reading. 282:15-22 not glossed («علمه الله» cannot be excerpted). STAGING v4: The written debt in a market: the creditor lends to the debtor on «تداينتم»; the scribe (seated) writes on «وليكتب» and «أن يكتب»; the debtor dictates on «وليملل» and lowers his head on «وليتق»; two witnesses come in on «واستشهدوا». The women witnesses, the weak or incapable debtor and his guardian are not drawn (a scroll plate for the guardian's dictation). Present trade: the debtor pays the trader on «تديرونها». Scales only for upright witnesses («ممن ترضون»), worldly justice, far from the Name; never the Mizan. STAGING v4: The written debt in a market: the creditor lends to the debtor on «تداينتم»; the scribe (seated) writes on «وليكتب» and «أن يكتب»; the debtor dictates on «وليملل» and lowers his head on «وليتق»; two witnesses come in on «واستشهدوا». The women witnesses, the weak or incapable debtor and his guardian are not drawn (a scroll plate for the guardian's dictation). Present trade: the debtor pays the trader on «تديرونها». Scales only for upright witnesses («ممن ترضون»), worldly justice, far from the Name; never the Mizan. STAGING v4: The written debt in a market: the creditor lends to the debtor on «تداينتم»; the scribe (seated) writes on «وليكتب» and «أن يكتب»; the debtor dictates on «وليملل» and lowers his head on «وليتق»; two witnesses come in on «واستشهدوا». The women witnesses (the camera stays on the creditor during that clause, away from the two men witnesses), the weak or incapable debtor and his guardian are not drawn (a scroll plate for the guardian's dictation). Present trade: the debtor pays the 